81 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 53 0 R
/T (Completely Fair Scheduler \(CFS\): shares CPU time among runnable processes using virtual runtime. It supports fairness but does not by itself guarantee low web-request latency; worker count, CPU limits and workload must be tuned. Page cache keeps recently accessed file data in RAM and reduces disk reads. Under pressure, cache pages may be reclaimed. Swapping moves less-used anonymous pages to disk; it can avoid immediate memory exhaustion but heavy swapping causes severe latency. /proc provides runtime process/kernel information such as /proc/meminfo, /proc/loadavg and /proc/PID/status. /sys exposes device, driver and kernel-object information. These are virtual interfaces, not ordinary persistent directories. Use free, vmstat, top and iostat to interpret them.)
/E (Completely Fair Scheduler \(CFS\): shares CPU time among runnable processes using virtual runtime. It supports fairness but does not by itself guarantee low web-request latency; worker count, CPU limits and workload must be tuned. Page cache keeps recently accessed file data in RAM and reduces disk reads. Under pressure, cache pages may be reclaimed. Swapping moves less-used anonymous pages to disk; it can avoid immediate memory exhaustion but heavy swapping causes severe latency. /proc provides runtime process/kernel information such as /proc/meminfo, /proc/loadavg and /proc/PID/status. /sys exposes device, driver and kernel-object information. These are virtual interfaces, not ordinary persistent directories. Use free, vmstat, top and iostat to interpret them.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
