/T (A Windows solution could use Windows Server with IIS or a reverse proxy, Windows services, Event Viewer, NTFS ACLs, PowerShell automation and Windows Firewall. Windows may suit teams with existing Microsoft expertise and applications, but its base memory/disk footprint is generally larger than a minimal Linux server. Automation time depends on staff skills: PowerShell is capable, while Bash is convenient for Linux operations. Windows Server licence cost depends on edition, cores and licensing terms; Linux distributions commonly avoid per-server OS licence fees, though support costs may apply. Compare measured resource use and total ownership cost rather than assuming one platform is always faster.)
/E (A Windows solution could use Windows Server with IIS or a reverse proxy, Windows services, Event Viewer, NTFS ACLs, PowerShell automation and Windows Firewall. Windows may suit teams with existing Microsoft expertise and applications, but its base memory/disk footprint is generally larger than a minimal Linux server. Automation time depends on staff skills: PowerShell is capable, while Bash is convenient for Linux operations. Windows Server licence cost depends on edition, cores and licensing terms; Linux distributions commonly avoid per-server OS licence fees, though support costs may apply. Compare measured resource use and total ownership cost rather than assuming one platform is always faster.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [11]
>>
