/E (VMs isolate operating systems, consolidate workloads, support snapshots for testing/rollback and may support live migration when storage/network/platform requirements are met. Costs include guest OS memory and disk, virtual I/O overhead, management complexity and possible licences. The portal and database can be separated into VMs where isolation is valuable, with reserved capacity and tested backups.)
