112 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 54 0 R
/T (VirtualBox is convenient for desktop labs and testing. A type-2 hypervisor adds the host OS between guest and hardware. CPU-bound tasks may run reasonably with hardware support, while I/O-bound tasks can experience extra storage/network layers. The host OS consumes RAM that cannot be allocated to guests. KVM is generally a stronger production choice for server consolidation and management; VirtualBox is suitable for development demonstrations.)
/E (VirtualBox is convenient for desktop labs and testing. A type-2 hypervisor adds the host OS between guest and hardware. CPU-bound tasks may run reasonably with hardware support, while I/O-bound tasks can experience extra storage/network layers. The host OS consumes RAM that cannot be allocated to guests. KVM is generally a stronger production choice for server consolidation and management; VirtualBox is suitable for development demonstrations.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
