/T (Assign private static addresses to application/database nodes and a public load-balancer address for users. Configure DNS such as results.example.edu. Nginx terminates TLS and proxies to the app on a private interface. Firewall: allow TCP 80/443 from users; allow SSH 22 only from the administration VPN/IP range; deny other inbound traffic. Allow database port 5432 only from application nodes. Use SSH keys, disable password login and direct root login, and patch regularly.)
/E (Assign private static addresses to application/database nodes and a public load-balancer address for users. Configure DNS such as results.example.edu. Nginx terminates TLS and proxies to the app on a private interface. Firewall: allow TCP 80/443 from users; allow SSH 22 only from the administration VPN/IP range; deny other inbound traffic. Allow database port 5432 only from application nodes. Use SSH keys, disable password login and direct root login, and patch regularly.)
