/T (Recommended approach: hybrid deployment. Keep baseline workloads and development/test systems on university infrastructure using VMs and containers. Burst to public cloud for result-day demand using a load balancer, autoscaling portal replicas and managed database services. This avoids purchasing hardware for a short peak while preserving control of baseline services. Test encryption, data location, backups, identity, network connectivity, egress fees and failover before production.)
/E (Recommended approach: hybrid deployment. Keep baseline workloads and development/test systems on university infrastructure using VMs and containers. Burst to public cloud for result-day demand using a load balancer, autoscaling portal replicas and managed database services. This avoids purchasing hardware for a short peak while preserving control of baseline services. Test encryption, data location, backups, identity, network connectivity, egress fees and failover before production.)
