/Title (Bare metal can provide high performance and direct hardware access but is less flexible to isolate and scale. VMs provide OS-level separation but consume guest memory and disk. Containers start quickly and provide high density but share the host kernel. Use containers for stateless web replicas, VMs for legacy/stronger OS boundaries, and bare metal only where measured)
