/Title (Kernel: privileged core that manages processes, CPU scheduling, virtual memory, filesystems through the VFS, device drivers and networking. Applications request kernel services through system calls. System libraries such as glibc provide standard programming interfaces. The shell \(Bash\) interprets commands, pipes and scripts. Utilities such as ps, df, ip and systemctl support monitoring and administration.)
