/Title (Completely Fair Scheduler \(CFS\): shares CPU time among runnable processes using virtual runtime. It supports fairness but does not by itself guarantee low web-request latency; worker count, CPU limits and workload must be tuned. Page cache keeps recently accessed file data in RAM and reduces disk reads. Under pressure, cache pages may be reclaimed. Swapping moves less-used anonymous pages to disk; it can avoid immediate memory exhaustion but heavy swapping causes severe latency. /proc provides runtime process/kernel information such as /proc/meminfo, /proc/loadavg and /proc/PID/status. /sys exposes device, driver and kernel-object information. These are virtual interfaces, not ordinary persistent directories. Use free, vmstat, top and iostat to interpret them.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 714 0 R
>>
endobj
733 0 obj
<<
/Title (The directory hierarchy starts at /. Common paths: /etc configuration, /var/log logs, /home user files, /usr programs and libraries, /opt optional software, /tmp temporary files and /dev device nodes. The Virtual File System provides a common interface to filesystems such as ext4 and XFS. Permissions define read/write/execute for owner, group and others. Setuid runs a program with its file owner's effective identity and must be audited. sudo grants approved administrative commands. Run the portal as a dedicated non-root account.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 715 0 R
>>
endobj
