<<
/Title (Type-1 hypervisors run directly on hardware: KVM, VMware ESXi, Xen and Hyper-V. Type-2 hypervisors run as applications on a host OS: VirtualBox and VMware Workstation. Full virtualisation presents virtual hardware for an unmodified guest OS. Para-virtualisation uses guest-aware interfaces/drivers to reduce overhead. Intel VT-x and AMD-V provide CPU virtualisation support; IOMMU supports controlled device assignment.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 753 0 R
>>
